[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-31", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 31 — six inserts in the mix at 2536 / 3827 ops/s; the value order carried across writes and served to snapshot readers", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-31.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 31 - six inserts in the mix, and the value order learns to be carried across writes and to serve snapshot readers\n\n> Seed: iteration 30's S21 - more inserts so more of the stream is\n> verifiable. Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung SF1 subset; SUT levi,\n> driver judah over the LAN; impl :datalog.\n\n## Generate\n\n  INS1 (person profile), INS3 (comment like), INS6 (post), INS7 (comment)\n  join INS2/INS8, each with a covering read: IS1 shows the profile, IC07\n  on the comment's creator lists the liker, IS4 shows the post's date,\n  IS7 on the parent lists the comment.\n\n  Prediction, written first: INS6/INS7 touch message/creationDate, so\n  the ordered drive's per-attribute sorted cache (keyed by identity of\n  the :avet inner map) misses on every IC02/IC09/IS2 that follows a\n  write -- their p50s leave the 3-8 ms band.\n\n## Rank - three runs\n\n    run                       IC02   IC09   IS2   thru @ 8 slots\n    1. cache rebuilt on miss   33.8   34.0  30.3    511 (1024 at 61.6% on-time)\n    2. order carried, 1 ver.   98.8  101.8  97.9    352 (1024 at 2.7%)   <- WORSE\n    3. order carried, 16 ver.   3.8    7.2   3.4   2536 (2560 at 100%)\n\n  Run 1 held the prediction. Run 2 refuted the first fix: the order now\n  lived in datalog.index as a sorted-set carried across assert-quad /\n  retract-quad, but ONE version was tracked -- a snapshot reader a few\n  writes behind the head missed, rebuilt (into a sorted-set, dearer than\n  a vector sort) and untracked the head, so no later write could carry\n  either. Run 3: sixteen versions per attribute; readers find theirs by\n  identity, writers carry from any tracked version.\n\n  Tests (datalog e75df8c2, 129/302/0): two writes then a read with zero\n  rebuilds; a retract the same; a reader five writes behind the head\n  hits and does not untrack it -- fails with one version. kotobase-peer\n  on the pin 262/804/0.\n\n  Read-after-write also learned a shape: IC07 is a top-20 window, and a\n  like whose date is older than every row of a full window was pushed out\n  by later likes from the same stream -- counted as :outside-window (4\n  and 5 of ~283), never visible, never lost. 565/565 verifiable inserts\n  visible across both sweeps; 155 unverifiable (dependencies outside the\n  subset); 169,844 inserts applied by the SUT, heap 2.6 GB.\n\n    slots  rate  on-time%  thru/s    ins1-8 p50   is3   ic09\n      8    2560  100.00   2536.0     1.9-2.1      6.8   7.2    (13-op: 1960)\n     32    4096   96.60   3827.4     2.5          8.1   8.4    (13-op: 3791)\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - A cache written for a frozen db is wrong the moment a writer exists:\n    the serving shape is snapshot reads behind an advancing head, and\n    \"one version\" was iteration 19's assumption made visible by\n    iteration 30's writes. The refutation of fix 1 was cheaper than\n    shipping it -- one sweep.\n  - Growth by widening on both slot columns, and the ordering reads are\n    back at their read-only latencies under a 6/17 write share.\n  - M2 stands at 6/8 inserts with read-after-write; INS4/INS5 (forums,\n    memberships) need IS6 to read them back; the simulation-time\n    interleave and the ACID suite are still the gap to \"updates\".\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: GROWTH (mix 13 -> 17 of 29 at\nhigher throughput on the same slots). Ratio to the audited No.1: 55 at\n8 slots, 36 at 32 -- raw.\n\nSeeds for iteration 32, in order:\n\n  - S22 (interleave): schedule inserts by the stream's simulation time\n    under the reads' TCR, honouring the dependency time -- the certified\n    driver's shape; the SUT's `:updates-applied` becomes a rate.\n  - S23 (INS4/INS5 + IS6): forums and memberships, and IS6 reads them.\n  - On decision: ADR-2609121100 (singleton counterparts), then SF1 proper\n    on levi with the whole mix.\n"}]
